       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and dangerous heart rhythm changes. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't make that dose safe. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. A finance office request isn't an appropriate source.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose and enter or authorize the order. If they confirm a dose within the normal range, usually 25\u2013200 mg once daily by mouth, I can enter it with that confirmation."
